<p><span class="font-semibold" data-streamdown="strong">Why two lines, not one:</span> the first is a fallback for older Safari, the second is the standard version. Browsers that understand <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">calc</code> ignore the first and use the second. Change both so they stay in sync — if you change only one, some browsers will render a different width from others.</p>
<h2 class="mt-6 mb-2 font-semibold text-2xl" data-streamdown="heading-2">Step 4 — Find the <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">body</code> rule</h2>
<p>Search for:</p>
